      "document_hash": "5e17867b5332c625220263d423782359fc07c317525c80ab10e1de0cd1fbc744",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5e17867b5332-0000-0001",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "ERIC GRANT, ESQ., Sacramento, Cal.; on behalf of the Petitioner."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2006-05-593",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5e17867b5332c625220263d423782359fc07c317525c80ab10e1de0cd1fbc744",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5e17867b5332-0000-0002",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "DOUGLAS HALLWARD-DRIEMEIER, ESQ., Assistant to the Solicitor General, Department of Justice, Washington, D.C.; on behalf of the Respondents."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Eric Grant)",
      "case_id": "2006-05-593",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5e17867b5332c625220263d423782359fc07c317525c80ab10e1de0cd1fbc744",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5e17867b5332-0000-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The court of appeals misinterpreted the Westfall Act in a way that unfairly deprives tort plaintiffs of the most basic procedural protections routinely afforded in both Federal and State courts."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2006-05-593",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5e17867b5332c625220263d423782359fc07c317525c80ab10e1de0cd1fbc744",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5e17867b5332-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Why is it a wholly State law claim if the principal matter is whether this Federal employee is immune from suit?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Eric Grant)",
      "case_id": "2006-05-593",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5e17867b5332c625220263d423782359fc07c317525c80ab10e1de0cd1fbc744",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5e17867b5332-0000-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Government has conceded that if Respondent Barry Haley acted as alleged in the complaint he was acting outside the course and scope of his Federal employment."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Grant (Government)",
      "case_id": "2006-05-593",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5e17867b5332c625220263d423782359fc07c317525c80ab10e1de0cd1fbc744",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5e17867b5332-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. GRANT: The Attorney General's submission, the Government's submission in the district court was that nothing happened."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2006-05-593",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5e17867b5332c625220263d423782359fc07c317525c80ab10e1de0cd1fbc744",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5e17867b5332-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: Well, why can't they do that, which is just what Wood says they can do, if anybody, you know, thinks that's valid? But the -- what's the problem then?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Hallward-Driemeier",
      "case_id": "2006-05-593",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5e17867b5332c625220263d423782359fc07c317525c80ab10e1de0cd1fbc744",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5e17867b5332-0001-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. HALLWARD-DRIEMEIER: That's right. And that's what the Attorney General did here, certified that Mr. Haley was acting within the scope of his employment at the time of the incident out of which the claim arose."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2006-05-593",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5e17867b5332c625220263d423782359fc07c317525c80ab10e1de0cd1fbc744",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5e17867b5332-0001-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 33,
        "start": 33
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: What does that mean? Does that mean that if the district court finds that in fact the defendant was not acting within the scope of his employment, the United States is eliminated as the defendant and the individual employee is resubstituted?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Hallward-Driemeier",
      "case_id": "2006-05-593",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5e17867b5332c625220263d423782359fc07c317525c80ab10e1de0cd1fbc744",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5e17867b5332-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. HALLWARD-DRIEMEIER: That is true. But I think that the intent of Congress was the same as this Court, all the members of this Court, recognized in Lamagno. In Lamagno, even the dissenters, the plurality, all acknowledged what Congress intended by the \"conclusive for purposes of removal\" language was to prevent the shuttling back and forth of the case. Once it was removed, it was to stay in Federal court. That was what Congress intended."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2006-05-593",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5e17867b5332c625220263d423782359fc07c317525c80ab10e1de0cd1fbc744",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5e17867b5332-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOUTER: Is that fair?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2006-05-593",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5e17867b5332c625220263d423782359fc07c317525c80ab10e1de0cd1fbc744",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5e17867b5332-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: But in my case I guess I don't think it ever gets to district court because there's no certification, but then the employee can ask the State court to have a bench trial on the scope of employment. Am I right about that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2006-05-593",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5e17867b5332c625220263d423782359fc07c317525c80ab10e1de0cd1fbc744",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5e17867b5332-0002-0003",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 50,
        "start": 50
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "(Whereupon, at 11:04 a.m., the case in the above-entitled matter was submitted.)"
    },
